==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The flow of the stage is very similar to Chapters 1 & 2 with plenty of peons at the start to farm Worker Cat levels. B.B.Bunny and Shibalien can give you at least 3 levels before more threatening enemies spawn.

This level shouldn't be much of a pain if you have decent Anti-Alien Treasures activated and a couple Red killers to get money from the One Horns.

Zigge is not a difficult zombie enemy and she doesn't burrow too far so this stage is more about how well you can deal with the main threats.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Zuche is the real issue in this stage. He spawns constantly and his early arrival always keeps you pushed to your base. This also means you have no real time to stall and can only get a Worker Cat level or two before you need something to remove its 34k area DPS from the map.

When Ursamajor spawns you should focus on him instead of One Horn because One Horn is very slow. Anti-Alien units and treasures are highly recommended so that the Ursamajor is less of a pain and you can focus on the Zuches.

One Horn is free money when he reaches you so you can finally summon all your heavy hitters.

The Zuches will likely not stop spawning before the base is destroyed. Once the Ursamajor dies it becomes a base race so send out everything!!

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Spawn a couple fast meatshields early to keep The Thrillerz from burrowing up to your base. This will also force the first Zuche to burrow early and save you some trouble.
*There is basically no time to save up at the beginning of this stage plus you only get 2 total peons to fight before your first Zuche appears. This makes the Rich Cat item a great choice.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] with Target Alien and Money Up talents can be a lifesaver on this match up. The inherent Red targeting will help with the One Horn too.
Once Zuche appears you need to have a threat on the board to deal with him, preferably a hard hitting Zombie Killer or he will just respawn and become a nuisance. You will be constantly fighting a Zuche, they keep spawning until the Ursamajor dies so don't let your guard down. Add The Thrillerz into the mix and your anti-Zombie game needs to be strong for this stage.

However, your Anti-Alien game needs to be even stronger. When you combine the heavy damage from Ursamajor with the Weaken effect from Calamary and Cyberhorn's massive health pool, you're going to want either some Weaken effects or some Freeze effects for this stage. Thaumaturge is pretty useless due to its long attack animation and short range for this match up. Weaken-Talent Corrupted Psychocat, Fire Squad Kachiyama, and Lumina are good examples of anti-Alien Weaken units which may help you if you own them.

Calamary should be handled similarly to in regular Chapter 3. Bring any LD units that outrange her to the fight. Unfortunately getting inside her range is tough due to the Ursamajor and Cyberhorn so the long route is the safest and most efficient option.

The One Horn is free money if you have a unit that can target Red and Alien or Red and Zombie. If not, just getting it with regular units with 350+ range like Dragon Cat is a good idea. If you find the combo of Cyberhorn, Calamary, and Ursamajor to be too much to handle, collect more alien treasures and try again later. The stage can appear again while you complete more and more of them.

